WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.235
Welcome to Part 6: test before you leave.

2
00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:08.890
This part is about the meters. How to
set them, where to take each reading,

3
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:11.927
and what to do when a
number doesn't make sense.

4
00:00:13.077 --> 00:00:15.533
If you didn't measure
it, it isn't finished.

5
00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:21.201
Two readings on every circuit. Amps,
and volts. It takes about ten minutes.

6
00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:25.820
Before you start, set the whole
system to PW, full bright.

7
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.967
Test A. Amps, with the clamp meter.

8
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:33.425
Set it to DC amps. Our lights run on DC.

9
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:37.543
On the AC setting, it
won't read anything useful.

10
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:40.877
With the jaws closed,
and away from any wire,

11
00:00:40.877 --> 00:00:43.757
press zero. Now it starts from nothing.

12
00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:49.782
Clamp around the positive feeder of
one circuit, at the box. One wire only.

13
00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:53.782
Clamp both wires together, and
they cancel each other out.

14
00:00:53.782 --> 00:00:55.691
You'll read close to zero.

15
00:00:55.991 --> 00:01:00.235
Close the jaws all the way, keep
the wire in the middle, and read it.

16
00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:04.299
Write it next to that circuit's
number. Then do every circuit.

17
00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:08.482
Test B. Volts, with the multimeter.

18
00:01:08.782 --> 00:01:13.590
Set it to DC volts. Red lead on the
positive, black on the negative.

19
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.410
First, the beginning. Meter the supply
output. It should read about 24 volts.

20
00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.910
Then the end. Meter at the
last light of each group.

21
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:26.544
That's the far end of the
run, not the injection point.

22
00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:30.257
Test at both. The beginning
tells you the supply is right.

23
00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:32.919
The end tells you the run isn't too long.

24
00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:38.150
A minus sign in front of the number just
means the leads are swapped. Flip them.

25
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.861
When a reading doesn't make sense, check
the meter before you blame the lights.

26
00:01:44.161 --> 00:01:48.828
Close to zero amps on a circuit
that's lit? You've clamped both wires,

27
00:01:48.828 --> 00:01:50.545
or the meter is on AC.

28
00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:56.385
Every circuit reading low for its light
count? Check the app is really on PW,

29
00:01:56.385 --> 00:01:59.080
full bright. Not BW, not a colour.

30
00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.865
Supply reads fine, but the last light
is low? The injection is too far away.

31
00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:08.291
Move it closer, or add
one, then test again.

32
00:02:08.591 --> 00:02:13.871
The supply itself reads well under 24
volts? Stop, and call your crew lead.

33
00:02:15.021 --> 00:02:16.077
Then write it down.

34
00:02:16.377 --> 00:02:19.673
For each circuit, the light
count, the amps on PW,

35
00:02:19.673 --> 00:02:24.339
the volts at the last light, and
the result against the field card.

36
00:02:24.639 --> 00:02:27.357
It goes in the test
sheet in the job files,

37
00:02:27.357 --> 00:02:30.263
with the address, your name, and the date.

38
00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:34.368
A tight circuit gets a note, so
nobody adds lights to it later.

39
00:02:35.518 --> 00:02:36.542
Let's lock it in.

40
00:02:36.842 --> 00:02:43.081
Clamp meter on DC amps, zeroed, around
the positive feeder only, at the box.

41
00:02:43.381 --> 00:02:47.975
Multimeter on DC volts, at
the beginning and at the end.

42
00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:52.737
About 24 at the supply, 22.8
or more at the last light.

43
00:02:53.037 --> 00:02:56.292
Odd reading? Check the
meter and the app first.

44
00:02:56.592 --> 00:03:00.164
Every reading goes in the
test sheet in the job files.

45
00:03:00.464 --> 00:03:06.206
Next, take the Part 6 quiz. Part
7, the last part, is older systems.
